A seat that advertises the keyboard capability and never sends a keymap
terminates the browser on the first modifiers event.

phoc, and every wlroots compositor a handheld runs, has to advertise
wl_seat's keyboard capability because the on-screen keyboard needs it. A
phone has no physical keyboard, so no wl_keyboard.keymap event is ever
sent. The protocol trace on a Pixel 2 XL is:

    wl_seat#30.capabilities(6)                     # keyboard|touch
     -> wl_seat#30.get_keyboard(new id wl_keyboard#9)
    wl_keyboard#9.enter(842, wl_surface#36, array[0])
    wl_keyboard#9.modifiers(843, 0, 0, 0, 0)

with no keymap event in between. WaylandKeyboard::OnModifiers() forwards
that straight to XkbKeyboardLayoutEngine::UpdateModifiers(), which
dereferences an xkb_state that was never built:

    #0  xkb_state_update_mask (libxkbcommon.so.0 + 0x23b34)  SEGV_MAPERR

Every launch, before a window appears. XkbLookup() in the same file
already returns early on a null state; these two entry points did not.
GTK tolerates a null keymap, which is why GTK browsers have never shown
this and Chromium always does.

--- a/ui/events/ozone/layout/xkb/xkb_keyboard_layout_engine.cc
+++ b/ui/events/ozone/layout/xkb/xkb_keyboard_layout_engine.cc
@@ -966,6 +966,17 @@
                                              uint32_t latched,
                                              uint32_t locked,
                                              uint32_t group) {
+  // A seat may advertise the keyboard capability and never send a keymap. A
+  // handheld running a wlroots compositor does exactly that: the on-screen
+  // keyboard needs wl_seat to carry the keyboard capability, while the device
+  // has no physical keyboard for a wl_keyboard.keymap event to describe. The
+  // first wl_keyboard.modifiers event then arrives before SetCurrentLayout*()
+  // has built any state, and dereferencing it terminates the browser during
+  // startup. XkbLookup() below already returns early for the same reason.
+  if (!xkb_state_) {
+    return 0;
+  }
+
   auto* state = xkb_state_.get();
   xkb_state_update_mask(state, depressed, latched, locked, 0, 0, group);
   auto component = static_cast<xkb_state_component>(XKB_STATE_MODS_DEPRESSED |
@@ -985,6 +996,11 @@
